{"labs": [{"id": 0, "type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "title": "", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn6le02ob03re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "Between the years 1946 and 1952, Eva Peron, famously called Evita, served as Argentina's First Lady. Evita was passionate about cinema and acting, so she boldly left her home to study and hopefully become a famous actress.", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn6le02ob03re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "In search of the bright lights, Eva moved to the big city at 15. Her acting debut was in 1935 when she naturally joined a theatre company. Her real breakthrough came when she became a high-paid radio actress with Radio Belgrano where she signed a five-year contract.", "id": 2, "time": "19000", "image": "engenn6le02ob03re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "While she was working as a radio actress, she met Juan Peron. One year later they were married. In 1946 Eva became Argentina's First Lady. She was charismatic, fiery, and immensely popular. The country's poor adored her and gave her the nickname Evita. After her death at 33, her  rags-to-riches story went on to become the subject of movies, books and musicals. Eventually, little Evita from the village became famous around the world.", "id": 3, "time": "38500", "image": "engenn6le02ob03re2img03.jpg"}], "audiosrc": "engenn6le02ob03re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn6le02ob03re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "_data": [], "type": "audio", "template_override": 1}], "exercises": [{"id": 0, "type": "WLC", "questions": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "I can describe people I admire. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can talk about people's past experiences. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can talk about how something happens or how someone behaves.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "Who are some